          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            7.
          %p
            This is one of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallelizable+manifold"} parallelizable
            spheres, as such corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            among the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras"} division algebras
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            structure but just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moufang+loop"} Moufang loop
            structure.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#QuaternionicHopfFibration Quaternionic Hopf fibration
          %p
            The 7-sphere participates in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+fibration"} Hopf fibration
            with the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            replaced by the division ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            or Hamiltonian numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 7
